# Paths git should pretend do not exist.
#
# Purpose: keep two categories out of the repository. Secrets, which must never
# be published. And anything regenerated from a checked-in file, since
# committing those causes conflicts and bloat for no benefit.

# Real configuration values. .env.example is the committed template instead.
.env

# Python: compiled bytecode caches, and the virtual environment, which is
# rebuilt from requirements.txt.
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Node: installed packages and build output, rebuilt from package.json.
node_modules/
.next/

# Finder metadata, of interest to nobody.
.DS_Store

# Files
ROADMAP.md